; preludes: form/form-stdlib/floor-lens.bml form/form-stdlib/model-registry.bml
; Expected: 31
; PROOF LEVEL: FKWU-STAGED — it preludes .bml and reads this Mac through the carrier.
;
; floor-spread-band — one sample cannot tell a dip from a step change.
;
; Taken from ivanfioravanti/ds4-metal#5 (BERARD David, merged 2026-09-08), whose harness
; interleaves every A/B and prints BOTH repeats — "-0.01% / -0.82%" — so a reader can see when a
; result did not hold still. This lens quoted ONE reading and a best-seen. On 2026-09-08 it read
; 6x low across every lane at once and the fall went into the tree as machine-wide with the cause
; unknown; on 2026-09-09 it read a new best. Neither reading could say whether the machine had
; changed or the sample had, and the whole floor stands on that number (corpus row 1421 onesample).
;
; Verdict 31:
;   1   three reads come back and every one of them is a real rate
;   2   the rate reported is the BEST of them — a slower read is something else asking at the
;       same time, not a lower floor
;   4   a triple that holds still is called still
;   8   a triple 6x apart — the shape of 2026-09-08 — is called WIDE, and the line says so in
;       words rather than leaving a reader to divide
;   16  the width is named in the text, both ends, so the number quoted can always be placed
(do
    (let blob (mr-path (mr-find "llama32-1b")))
    (let rd (fl-reads blob 3))
    (let c0 (if (and (eq (fl-read-n rd) 3) (and (gt (fl-read-lo rd) 0.0) (gt (fl-read-hi rd) 0.0))) 1 0))
    (let c1 (if (eq (fl-read-gbs rd) (fl-read-hi rd)) 2 0))
    (let tight (list 400.0 390.0 400.0 3))
    (let fallen (list 400.0 65.0 400.0 3))
    (let c2 (if (eq (fl-held-still? tight) 1) 4 0))
    (let c3 (if (eq (fl-held-still? fallen) 0) 8 0))
    (let c4 (if (and (ge (str_find (fl-spread-text fallen) "WIDE" 0) 0)
                (and (ge (str_find (fl-spread-text tight) "390" 0) 0)
                     (ge (str_find (fl-spread-text tight) "400" 0) 0))) 16 0))
    (add c0 (add c1 (add c2 (add c3 c4)))))
